is South, so no extra fan).  \n  - All Chows possible if you finish with chows.  \n  - No honors except F1 exposed, so All Simples possible if avoid terminals/honors.  \n  - But you already have W3-W4-W5 chow and F1 pung, so hand is mixed.  \n\n- Risk: Discarding a tile that others might win on or call.  \n  - Next player melds: T4-T5-T6, B1x3, W1-W2-W3 \u2192 they have many simples, may need terminals/honors?  \n  - Across player: W6-W7-W8, T1-T2-T3, T7-T8-T9 \u2192 they have bamboo and W chows, likely going for All Chows or Half Flush.  \n  - Previous player: B8x3, J3x3, T6-T7-T8 \u2192 they have dots and honors, possibly waiting on dots or honors.  \n\n**Promising moves:**  \n1. **Play T2** \u2013 T2 only 1 left in wall, safe because others have chows with T2? Across player already has T1-T2-T3 meld, so T2 is dead for them. Next player hasn\u2019t shown interest in T2. Low risk.  \n2. **Play B3** \u2013 B3 has 2 left, but previous player has dots meld (B8), might be waiting for dots? B3 is not connected strongly for you.  \n3. **Play T5** \u2013 T5 only 1 left, but next player has T4-T5-T6 meld already, so T5 is safe for them. Others? Unlikely.  \n4. **Play B6** \u2013 B6 has 2 left, isolated in your hand, safe.  \n5. **Play B7** \u2013 Keep B7 pair for potential pung (4 left), but discarding one B7 would break pair. Better keep.  \n6. **Play W4** \u2013 You have a pair, could pung later (2 left), but W4 is somewhat live (others have W chows). Discarding W4 might give someone a chow (W2-W3-W4 or W4-W5-W6).  \n\nBest: Discard the most isolated tile with least chance of helping opponents.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nT2 is safest: Across player already melded T1-T2-T3; next player hasn\u2019t collected T2; T2 only 1 left in wall, so almost no one can complete a meld with it.  \nT5 also safe but slightly more live (1 left, but someone could have T5 pair waiting).  \nB3/B6 are dots, previous player has B8 pung and T6-T7-T8, maybe collecting dots, so avoid dots if possible.  \